  "RightSideHtmlBlock": "<h4>Categorize and assess the incident</h4><p>Assign the category (precedence: CAT 1, 2, 4, 7, 3, 5, 6, 8, 9), then rate the technical impact (on the information network and IS machines) and the operational impact (on the ability to perform the mission) for each security objective. Only the impact is scored.</p><p><b>Reading the score.</b> Low = 1, Moderate = 10, High = 100: the hundreds digit counts High ratings, the tens Moderate, the units Low; the incident's impact is the highest non-zero digit.</p><p><b>Reporting timelines (Table C-A-1)</b></p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th>Category</th><th>Initial notification / initial report to next tier / initial JIMS submission</th><th>Minimum reporting</th></tr><tr><td>1 Root Level / 2 User Level Intrusion</td><td>High: 15 min / 4 h / 6 h; Moderate: 2 h / 8 h / 12 h; Low: 4 h / 12 h / 24 h</td><td>Tier I</td></tr><tr><td>4 Denial of Service</td><td>High: 15 min / 4 h / 6 h; Moderate: 15 min / 4 h / within 6 h of discovery; Low: as directed</td><td>Tier I</td></tr><tr><td>7 Malicious Logic</td><td>High: 15 min / 4 h / 6 h (Tier I); Moderate: 2 h / 8 h / 12 h; Low: as directed</td><td>Tier II</td></tr><tr><td>3 Unsuccessful Activity Attempt</td><td>Any: 4 h / 12 h / 24 h</td><td>Tier II</td></tr><tr><td>5 Non-Compliance Activity</td><td>4 h / 12 h / 48 h</td><td>Tier II</td></tr><tr><td>6 Reconnaissance</td><td>As directed</td><td>Tier II</td></tr><tr><td>8 Investigating</td><td>within 2 h (acknowledgement) / most severe possible interpretation / 24 h</td><td>Tier II</td></tr><tr><td>9 Explained Anomaly</td><td>N/A / 24 h / 72 h</td><td>Tier II</td></tr></table><p><i>Source: CJCSM 6510.01B, Cyber Incident Handling Program (10 July 2012, current as of 18 December 2014), Enclosure B Appendix A (Tables B-A-1, B-A-2), Enclosure C Appendix A (Table C-A-1), Enclosure D Appendix C (levels of impact). Approved for public release; distribution is unlimited.</i></p>",
